      :evidence "kotoba.compiler.affine in kotoba-sema (moved from kotoba-native, which is not on the dependency path of the frontend that decides, so the gate could never have been consulted from where the decision is made). The only caller is check-affine-writes!, and it calls linear? -- NOT linear-parameter? or linear-let-thread?, which no caller consults. 26 tests (measured, not carried over; 7 added 2026-09-01 for fused-rmw?). Conservative: refuses two uses on one path, a bare reference, the handle stored into itself, a consumed name that is read again, and treats vector-drop as CONSUMING because a view whose parent is later written in place is a view of something else."
      :shapes-admitted #{:let-threaded-through-distinct-names
