      :evidence "kotoba-wasm emits kotoba:typed/vector-assoc-in-place-i64 for the head; confirmed in the compiled module import list."
      :end-to-end "Measured 2026-09-01 on amu agent/linear-vector-host d40236be: source admitted, module imports kotoba:typed/vector-alloc-i64 and vector-assoc-in-place-i64, main() returns 16n on browser-host.mjs. The frozen-array objection was resolved by exempting linear handles from the frozen check via a linearValues WeakSet, which also lets the per-operation scan skip them -- that scan, not the copy, was the other O(n)."
      :js-kotoba-v1 "Lowered as of kotoba-script b72a333 (2026-09-01), landed in amu #732. It knew neither head that morning, which is why the three-way corpus could not carry a positive vector: that suite requires the KIR reference, the restricted ESM and the wasm to AGREE, and one of the three could not compile the program. The runtime needed the same carve-out browser-host did -- assertVectorI64 is makeVector, which freezes and re-asserts every element, so it was doing O(length) work on every operation whether or not that operation copied. A linear handle is exempt from both, by identity in a WeakSet rather than by shape."
